<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al Qasimi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Qawasim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Al Qasimi, or Qawasim, are an Arab dynasty and tribal confederation of the southern Gulf, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras-al-khaimah">Ras al-Khaimah</a> and Sharjah. In the 18th century they built a maritime power on both shores of the Gulf, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> attacked in 1809 and 1819 in campaigns against alleged piracy, leading to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/general-maritime-treaty-of-1820">General Maritime Treaty of 1820</a>. Branches of the family still rule Sharjah and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras">Ras</a> al-Khaimah.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-qasimi.jpg" alt="Al Qasimi" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Madden · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Sharjah_and_Ras_Al_Khaimah.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
